           Well, there are those of you who have been hanging around the North Gate of Qeynos and wondering, what's up with the guy complaining about his bad back.  Well, that was me trying to work out the kinks in the quest I've been trying to run.  Unfortunatly, I didn't realize that the dialog that I was entering into my hot buttons wasn't being compleatly heard.  I have ironed out some of the bugs, but I still need help.<br>
          <br>
           First, I need someone who have a very good understanding of how to set up the social buttons to deliver the dialog that I need for this and future quest/events.  It's much easier if I have these dialogs set up ahead of time, so I can just hit a button to answer a <KEYWORD>.<br>
          <br>
           Second, I need people who are willing to take an hour or so of their time to help iron out some of the plot wrinkles that may bug a quest/event.  Those who do will recieve credit if I am able to ever get Verant to imp the quest for real.<br>
          <br>
           And Finally!  I need donations to make these quest events tempting enough for people to particapate.  Currently, I've just been giving plat and inexpensive magic items as reward.  Even so, I don't have a large supply of these items, and last night I gave out 40 plat to those who helped me get tis far.  (Thanks Lanamder, Chukulan, Azudel, Rotomis, and the couple others I forgot to write down in the beginning)  That may not be much to some people, but to a lowbie such as myself, it hits the pocket book.<br>
          <br>
           To the people who ask why I'm doing this.  It's because I'm an old school RPer (that means from the days of the pen and paper games), and the everyday hack and slash becomes boring after a while, so I decided to try this for a little bit.  I am making no profit from this, just a sence of accomplishment from seeing a low level character run off on a quest.  One thing I have learned though, is that it's not easy standing in one spot playing the part of NPC for two or more hours.<br>
          <br>
          Anyone crazy enough to help out, please contact me (Rali) in game or at mlchrist@yahoo.com<br>

